 ### [Multi-stage Training with Pose Prediction](15018-multi-stage-training-with-pose-prediction.md)
-Multi-stage training with pose prediction is a progressive optimization strategy for feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting that decouples geometry learning from pose estimation to stabilize training. It solves the problem of error propagation in end-to-end differentiable rendering, where inaccuracies in predicted camera poses corrupt the learned Gaussian representation. Unlike single-stage approaches, it separates the process into distinct phases: initial pose-aware training, pose-free geometry refinement, and final end-to-end fine-tuning. This method is specifically designed for architectures that predict Gaussians from context views without ground-truth camera supervision during inference.
+A progressive strategy for feed-forward 3DGS that decouples geometry learning from pose estimation. It sets itself apart by separating training into pose-aware, pose-free, and end-to-end phases. Choose it for architectures predicting Gaussians from context views without ground-truth camera supervision during inference.
 
 ### [Free-View Training (FVT)](15162-free-view-training-fvt.md)
-Free-View Training (FVT) is a training strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that disentangles model performance from the specific number of input views, enabling robust novel view synthesis across broader view ranges regardless of input view count. It adds geometrical constraints on 3D Gaussian localization by supervising image renderings in broader view interpolations, significantly contributing to depth estimation and adaptation to longer input sequences. Unlike standard 3DGS which often overfits to the specific camera poses provided during training, FVT ensures generalizability by training on long sequences with randomly sampled context views.
+Disentangles model performance from the specific number of input views by training on long sequences with randomly sampled context views. It sets itself apart by ensuring generalizability across broader view ranges regardless of input count. Choose it when robust novel view synthesis across diverse viewpoints is required.
 
